# Engineering Protocol v2 (binding)

Full rules (§1–§60): `docs/03-development/ENGINEERING_PROTOCOL.md`
Quality gates: `docs/03-development/QUALITY_GATES.md`
Risk matrix: `docs/03-development/RISK_CLASSIFICATION.md`

## Rule priority when conflicts arise (§47)

Security → Human approval → ADRs → Protocol → Docs → Sprint scope → Preference

## Read order (§1)

`DEVELOPMENT_GUIDE.md` → `PROJECT_STATE.md` → `PROJECT_BACKLOG.md` → sprint → ADRs → task source only.

Confidence < 90% → stop and ask.

## Before non-trivial implementation (§39, §40, §59)

1. Definition of Ready satisfied (`templates/DEFINITION_OF_READY.md`)
2. Spec/plan approved — never code directly from a prompt
3. Risk classified (`RISK_CLASSIFICATION.md`)
4. Human approval if HIGH/CRITICAL or §41 triggers (`templates/HUMAN_APPROVAL_CHECKLIST.md`)
5. ADR compliance verified (§43) — conflict → STOP, write ADR first

## Workflow (§40)

Requirements → Clarification → Acceptance Criteria → Technical Plan → Implement → Verify → Document → Commit → Handover

## Before every commit (§6)

```bash
pnpm verify
```

## Task complete only when (§60)

DoR satisfied + DoD satisfied + acceptance criteria verified + quality gates + docs + evidence + rollback + handover.

## Forbidden for AI agents (§58)

Invent APIs/config/architecture/deps/conventions/undocumented behavior. Repository-wide refactors. Assume human approval. Violate ADRs silently.

## Session end (§16)

Update `PROJECT_STATE`, `PROJECT_BACKLOG`, `CHANGELOG`, append `PROJECT_HANDOVER`.

## Executable governance

Complete `docs/03-development/GOVERNANCE_CHECKLIST.md` every session. CI: `.github/workflows/governance.yml`.
